SQSO-EPS-BRD-001 electrical rule check (SKiDL 3.0 ERC), generated by design.py

No errors or warnings found while running ERC.


Waivers (intentional modelling choices, reviewed):
W1  MSP430FR2355 port pins are typed PASSIVE: their direction is set by the EPS-controller firmware.
W2  Multi-pin outputs of one device (TPS1H100 OUT5-7, TPS16630 OUT17-18) have one POWER-OUT pin; the others are
    PASSIVE, so the checker does not report the device driving its own net.
W3  Power nets fed through passive elements (FETs, fuses, shunts, switches, connectors) are declared driven
    (net.drive = POWER): the pack and string nets, switched rails and the one-shot supplies (BXP_*, SET_REQ,
    RST_REQ, which are logic outputs powering a 35 nA timer).
W4  Pins marked NOCONNECT are left open on purpose (datasheet NC pins, unused AFE outputs DCHG/DDSG/PDSG/REG2,
    TPS16630 MODE open = latch-off, TPS1H000 DELAY open = default, INA3221 alert outputs, unused MCU ports).
W5  The OBC I2C2 pull-ups are on the OBC board (ICD-001 section 2.2); the EPS adds none on I2C2_SCL/SDA.
